A **TRD (Technical Requirements Document)** describes **how the system will be built**. While the PRD focuses on business requirements and features, the TRD covers architecture, technologies, APIs, database design, security, deployment, testing, and implementation details.

---

# Technical Requirements Document (TRD)

## MediaShelf – Personal Movie & Book Library Management System

**Version:** 1.0
**Project Type:** Full-Stack MERN Web Application
**Architecture:** Client–Server (3-Tier)
**Database:** MongoDB

---

# 1. Purpose

The purpose of this document is to define the technical architecture, implementation strategy, database schema, API specifications, security measures, and development standards for the MediaShelf application.

---

# 2. System Architecture

```text
+-------------------------+
|      React Client       |
| (React + Tailwind CSS)  |
+------------+------------+
             |
        REST API (HTTPS)
             |
+------------+------------+
|   Express.js API Server |
| Authentication          |
| Business Logic          |
| Validation              |
+------------+------------+
             |
          Mongoose ODM
             |
+------------+------------+
|       MongoDB Atlas     |
+-------------------------+
```

Architecture Pattern:

* Client-Server Architecture
* REST API
* MVC Pattern
* Component-Based Frontend

---

