# 9. REST APIs

## Authentication

POST /api/auth/register

POST /api/auth/login

GET /api/auth/profile

POST /api/auth/logout

---

## Library

GET /api/items

GET /api/items/:id

POST /api/items

PUT /api/items/:id

DELETE /api/items/:id

---

## Favorites

PATCH /api/items/:id/favorite

GET /api/favorites

---

## Dashboard

GET /api/dashboard

---

## Analytics

GET /api/analytics

---

## Upload

POST /api/upload

---

# 10. API Response Format

Success

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Movie added successfully",
  "data": {}
}
```

Failure

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": []
}
```

---

# 11. Business Logic

### Add Movie

Validate Input

↓

Save to MongoDB

↓

Return Success

↓

Refresh Dashboard

---

### Favorite

User clicks Heart

↓

Update MongoDB

↓

Update Dashboard

↓

Update Favorites Page

↓

Update Navbar Badge

No Refresh Required

---

### Search

User types

↓

Backend receives query

↓

MongoDB Regex Search

↓

Separate

Movies

Books

↓

Return Results

---

# 12. Search Algorithm

Fields

* Title
* Genre
* Description
* Author
* Tags

MongoDB

```javascript
{
 title: {
   $regex: keyword,
   $options: "i"
 }
}
```

---

# 13. Filtering

Support

Movie

Book

Genre

Rating

Status

Release Year

Favorite

---

# 14. Sorting

Movies

Newest

Oldest

Rating

Alphabetical

Books

Newest

Oldest

Rating

Alphabetical

Sorting should be independent.

---

# 15. Pagination

Movies

Independent Pagination

Books

Independent Pagination

Changing Movie page must never change Book page.

---

# 16. Theme Management

Use React Context.

Store theme

```text
light

dark
```

Persist using Local Storage.

---

# 17. State Management

Use React Context API for

* Authentication
* Theme
* Favorites

Use local component state where appropriate.

