# 24. Deployment

Frontend

* Vercel

Backend

* Render or Railway

Database

* MongoDB Atlas

Environment Variables

```env
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=<mongodb_connection_string>
JWT_SECRET=<jwt_secret>
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173
```

---

# 25. Non-Functional Requirements

* Responsive on Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile
* Page load under 2 seconds on a standard broadband connection
* RESTful API design
* Modular, reusable components
* Accessible UI (WCAG-friendly)
* Scalable folder structure
* Maintainable codebase
* Consistent API response format
* Secure authentication and authorization
* Production-ready deployment configuration

---

# 26. Future Enhancements

* Cloudinary integration for poster storage
* TMDB API integration for movie metadata
* Google Books/Open Library API integration for book metadata
* AI-based recommendations
* Barcode/ISBN scanning
* Progressive Web App (offline support)
* Reading and watch progress tracking
* Push notifications for reminders
* Docker containerization and CI/CD pipeline

This TRD provides the technical blueprint needed to implement the MediaShelf project in a structured, maintainable, and production-ready manner.
